            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Derek Howard",
                        "email": "derekh@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "derekhoward55"
                    },
                    "message": "High level question - are there any design updates for multi-chassis, eg in the readme or somewhere?  I believe most of our other apps have updated the designs in the readme/doc files.\n\nAre these changes in this commit basically just moves of routines/function from the psu_manager files to the chassis files?  Any new code that we should focus the review on?\n\nIs the plan to remove the copied routines/function from the psu_manager files at some later point, when the chassis files are compiled in?  How are you keeping track of what will need to be removed from the psu_manager files?\n\nLine 8 of commit message ends with ':' instead of '.' like the rest.\n\nMinoe: In general, the commit message contains a mix of past and present tense... I'd recommend being consistent.  Eg \"Read initial... and sets...\" - should be either \"Reads...sets\" or \"Read..set\".  Eg in Test section, \"Verified\" and \"validate\" mix tense - should probably be \"Verified\"/\"Validated\" since it looks like you are saying \"The following tests _were_ done in a simulated environment.\n\nThanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "I will investigate if the design I had needs any update.\n\nYes, some routines moved from psu_manager with minor changes to work with multi chassis.\n\nThe psu_manager code will not be used in the future. Keeping track of what's removed/needed by comparing the logic.\n\nWill change test section of the commit message."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Looks good. I had two comments, but they are for larger changes that should probably done in future commits."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.cpp",
                    "line": 975,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "There are many places in this file where it uses the D-Bus path constant POWER_OBJ_PATH, which corresponds to \"/org/openbmc/control/power0\". That path represents the state of the entire system and not a specific chassis. See phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md for more information.\n\nI realize you copied this code from psu_manager.cpp, and that code only supported a single-chassis system. So you didn't make a mistake.\n\nBut this class will eventually need to change to use the chassis-specific D-Bus path. For chassis 1 the path will be \"/org/openbmc/control/power1\", for chassis 2 \"/org/openbmc/control/power2\", etc.\n\nIt is fine not to make the change yet. I haven't changed the phosphor-power-sequencer application to publish these new paths yet. Hopefully in the next month or two that will be supported.\n\nI would suggest in the future creating a commit that makes this change in all the appropriate places once the phosphor-power-sequencer enhancement is done. Please add that to your to do list."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.cpp",
                    "line": 975,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "Added a note to fix this when phosphor-power-sequencer change."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.cpp",
                    "line": 1003,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "You will eventually need to add the chassis number to this message (e.g. \"Chassis 2: Failed to ...\"). We need to know which chassis hit the error. That is probably true for all or nearly all the journal messages in this class and the PowerSupply class.\n\nI would suggest creating a commit in the future that fixes all these at once in a consistent way. Please add this to your to do list."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.cpp",
                    "line": 1003,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "The fix will be future fix"
                }
            ],
